data/hashing/xxhash64/

xxh64.txt holds the XXH64 test vectors of the xxHash repository by Yann
Collet, https://github.com/Cyan4973/xxHash, from the array
XSUM_XXH64_testdata of tests/sanity_test_vectors.h on the branch dev at commit
215108c62f84a9a94d1e821800b29963f544a602, downloaded on 2026-10-25, SHA-256
e81b5f30744714293c511110b0b6f538516d9432153d8a1cb7dc0d8a73589af7.
extract.py wrote each entry { len, seed, result } as the line "len seed
result", with the seed and the result in lowercase hexadecimal; the file is
otherwise a copy of the entries in their order.  LICENSE is the repository's
license file, the BSD 2-Clause License, which covers this material.

Each vector hashes the first len bytes of a buffer that tests/sanity_test.c
of the same commit fills by the generator of its function fillTestBuffer:
byteGen starts at 2654435761, and byte i is byteGen >> 56, after which byteGen
is multiplied by 11400714785074694797 modulo 2^64.  The vectors cover every
length from 0 to 4160 bytes with the seeds 0 and 0x9E3779B1.

The transcription follows doc/xxhash_spec.md of the same commit, "xxHash fast
digest algorithm", version 0.2.0 (29/06/23), SHA-256
61c47af338b2feefcc7621700ef6b941bcf9b1dd33899c503f68cb797e7ef333.
